nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-09-13T15:55:05Z","label":{"name":"priority/high","color":"ffdc5e"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1245973357","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884#issuecomment-1245973357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884","id":1245973357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5KRAtt","user":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-13T21:30:15Z","updated_at":"2022-09-13T21:30:15Z","body":"`yb_pg_alter_table` test is failing due to a server crash.\r\nThe crash occurs on line 285 of `yb_pg_alter_table.sql`: `select * from my_locks order by 1;`\r\nThe `my_locks` is a view type which retrieves lock mode from pg_locks table:\r\n```\r\ncreate or replace view my_locks as\r\nselect case when c.relname like 'pg_toast%' then 'pg_toast' else c.relname end, max(mode::lockmodes) as max_lockmode\r\nfrom pg_locks l join pg_class c on l.relation = c.oid\r\nwhere virtualtransaction = (\r\n        select virtualtransaction\r\n        from pg_locks\r\n        where transactionid = txid_current()::integer)\r\nand locktype = 'relation'\r\nand relnamespace != (select oid from pg_namespace where nspname = 'pg_catalog')\r\nand c.relname != 'my_locks'\r\ngroup by c.relname;\r\n```\r\nThe problematic query comes from the `virtualtransaction` subquery which attempts to retrieve the current transaction ID.\r\n\r\nWhen `select  txid_current();` query runs as a standalone, it reproduces the same server crash error.\r\nSame error occurs when the query runs inside a transaction block except when the transaction rollsback:\r\n ```\r\nbegin;\r\nselect  txid_current();\r\n txid_current \r\n--------------\r\n            5\r\n(1 row)\r\ncommit; -- server closed the connection unexpectedly\r\n\r\nbegin;\r\nselect  txid_current();\r\n txid_current \r\n--------------\r\n            6\r\n(1 row)\r\nrollback;\r\nROLLBACK \r\n```\r\n\r\nThe crash comes from a failed assertion in `procarray.c` inside `ProcArrayEndTransaction` function:\r\n```TRAP: FailedAssertion(\"!(!((allPgXact[proc->pgprocno].xid) != ((TransactionId) 0)))\", File: \"../../../../../../../src/postgres/src/backend/storage/ipc/procarray.c\", Line: 440)```\r\nThis function attempts to mark a postgres transaction as no longer running. \r\nIf the transaction ID passed from the caller is invalid, we first confirm the top-level transaction ID from the global process structure (ProcGlobal) is also invalid -- this is where it fails. Then it proceeds to clear out the member variables of the PGProc struct in shared memory.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1245973357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1248577513","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884#issuecomment-1248577513","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884","id":1248577513,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5Ka8fp","user":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-15T20:24:59Z","updated_at":"2022-09-15T20:24:59Z","body":"The second issue with `yb_pg_alter_table` test is the different output than the expected sql result.\r\nThis occurs when chains of sql files run prior to this alter sql test which are dependent commands.\r\nFor example:\r\n`onek_unique1` is an index created from `yb_pg_create_index.sql` file.\r\n`onek` is a table created from `yb_pg_create_table.sql` file.\r\n\r\nIn `yb_pg_alter_table.sql`, there are commands that tries to rename the above index, add/drop constraint and rename the above table. \r\nThe expected output used to work correctly for those sql commands until a change was added by another commit which changed the command outputs to return \"does not exist\" error instead.\r\nThe culprit commit was [adding support for CREATE STATISTICS statement](https://phabricator.dev.yugabyte.com/D18429) (please check in `yb_pg_alter_table.out` line 226 to 239).\r\nIt seems like the `yb_pg_alter_table` file was tested as a standalone which is why it expected the index and table to return the \"does not exist\" error. \r\nIn the detective, I see there are 3 builds that failed with `TestPgRegressTable` and 2 builds which failed to rebase so perhaps the test was dismissed.\r\n\r\nWe must revert the change to the original expected output result.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1248577513/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1248645862","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884#issuecomment-1248645862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13884","id":1248645862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5KbNLm","user":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-15T21:23:01Z","updated_at":"2022-09-15T21:27:19Z","body":"The third issue is in `yb_create_table.sql` test.\r\nThere's a section that connects to `\\c yugabyte` then creates a temporary table and view.\r\nThe creation of temporary table fails due to `restart read required` error:\r\n```\r\ncreate temporary table temp_tab(a int);\r\nERROR:  Query error: Restart read required at: { read: { physical: 1663169507084339 } local_limit: { physical: 1663169507084339 } global_limit: <min> in_txn_limit: <max> serial_no: 0 }\r\n```\r\nThe error comes from `async_rpc.cc`'s `CommonResponseCheck()` function.\r\nThe function checks against the ReadHybridTime using the response protobuf and checks whether `has_restart_read_time()` is set to true.\r\nIf so, this long string of error is created in `read_hybrid_time.h` demanding a read restart.\r\n\r\nThe error is not reproducible in ysql shell as the temporary table gets created without any issue.\r\nA possible workaround is to add a sleep thread immediately after `\\c yugabyte` to give some time for the tablet server which has skewed clock to correct itself then execute the temporary table creation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1248645862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"emhna","id":66644511,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ0NTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66644511?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna","html_url":"https://github.com/emhna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emhna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gith